    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0138" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/1537: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-07T18:00:00+02:00">June 7, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 7—4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1755. In light of wolfram settlement and as it appears improbable that we shall
                    be able to present supply purchase proposals immediately, <pb facs="0139"
                        n="129" xml:id="pg129"/> I believe it of considerable importance that we
                    provide Portuguese authorities within next few days with some tangible evidence
                    of our intention to give Portugal economic benefits in return for step which has
                    been taken. It is highly desirable also that a favorable atmosphere should
                    prevail during time when Portuguese will be formulating their wolfram control
                    regulations. Accordingly, I should like to inform them that we propose to cancel
                    all surcharges after June 30, if Department approves.</p>
                <p>Urgent reply to this cable is requested.</p>
                <p>British Embassy is sending a parallel cable to London.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; to London as 273; to Madrid by courier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
